This is stuff specific to www.rapidcow.org and friends

(In hopes of confusing less people, our branch lives in rc/main) 

= What to do next

We're on v1.19.1?????

git fetch origin
git merge v??????

do something like that idk

Then read INSTALL (it's a symlink to building-anubis.md, source of
the HTML document at anubis.techaro.lol/docs/developer/building-anubis/)

     => note: due to the way make rules there unconditionally run
        note: each other, you might as well run the ultimate target
        note: (it's called build or something i forgot)

     => note^2: there seems to be this new esbuild(1) command dependency?
        note^2: install it with `apt[-get] install esbuild'.
        note^2: edit: actually, don't.  these pesky fellas live in Node.js
	note^2: and so it's better to keep them out of /usr/bin.
	note^2: solved it by delegating execution to npx(1).

Then install -m755 var/anibus /usr/local/bin
(I almost forgot the executable bits -- very important)

    [[[ though you can you can do all of this with Make rules
       (just stay in this directory in that case; don't leave!) ]]]

reload is NOT a thing!!!! do systemctl restart
(also it's probably a good idea to enable anubis@nginx)

= systemd Linux

/run/anubis/ should exist!  Don't let rebooting eat it...

mkdir -m 755 /run/anubis/
chown anubis:anubis /run/anubis/

Make sure the anubis user can make a unix socket there

sudo -u anubis nc -U /run/anubis/foo.sock -l

    [[[ thankfully this is a normal enough question to get asked
        9 years ago: https://serverfault.com/questions/779634
        /create-a-directory-under-var-run-at-boot/779648#779648
        I'll give RuntimeDirectory a shot, hold on ]]]
